# See fixtures/101_match_faults.ds.
#
#   pump 1  a Sensor whose state is null and whose division traps, then a
#           Tick: `all_cool` and `no_div` stay blocked and `div_where` does
#           not fire; both traps are recorded, each after the assert whose
#           propagation raised it ([RFCS.6.7])
#   pump 2  the Sensor becomes cool and divisible (2 / 1 > 1.0): `all_cool`
#           fires; `no_div` stays blocked by a definite `true`; `div_where`
#           fires. Superseding the trapping Sensor ends its pairs, and a
#           retraction evaluates no join test ([IRET.7.7]), so no third trap
#           is recorded ([LERR.1.4.12])
assert Sensor entity_id=s1 state=null a=1 b=0
assert Tick id=1
pump
assert Sensor entity_id=s1 state=10.0 a=2 b=1
pump
